# data file for fldtk fluid (Fast Light User Interface Designer)
version 1.0000
comment {The interactive editor's own Settings dialog.

Ported from FLTK's fluid/panels/settings_panel.fl. Every one of FLTK's six tabs (General/Project/Layout/Shell/
Locale/User) is placed, at FLTK's own exact widget layout and
coordinates (the dialog itself is 360x585, matching FLTK
exactly). Project's header/code-file split
(this port generates one D file with no such split at all) has no
backing subsystem to wire to, so its widgets are placed, visible, and
interactive in
the sense that FLTK itself handles them (typing in an Input, clicking a
CheckButton), but their callbacks are deliberately left unwired (no
`callback`/`setup` property at all), matching this
project's own established two-pass `widget_panel.fl` precedent.
Layout and
User are both wired for real -- Project is the one tab still in that
placed-but-unwired state; each tab's own top comment below
names exactly what it's still missing.

What's genuinely wired to real, working subsystems: General's Scheme/
Tooltips/External-Editor controls (unchanged from before), "Show
Positioning Guides" (`gui_main.showGuides()`, applied to every open
window's canvas at once -- a project-wide display preference, not any
one window's own state, see that function's own doc comment), "Remember
Window Positions" (`gui_main.positionWindow()` gates its saved-x/y
restore on
`appPrefs` key `prev_window_pos`, matching FLTK's own `Application
::position_window()`'s `if (prevpos_button->value())` guard), "Open
Previous File on Startup" (checked at the very top of `gui_main.d`'s
startup sequence, matching FLTK's own `if (!c && openlast_button->
value() && history.abspath[0][0] && ...)`), "Show Comments in Browser"
(`fluid.node_browser.showComments`, consulted by the widget-tree
browser's own row layout/drawing), "
`fluid.project_history.History` already read this same `appPrefs` key;
the spinner's callback now calls a new `gui_main.reloadRecentFiles()`
to apply a change immediately), and "Show Completion Dialogs" (gates a
success-only `fl.message()` popup at the tail of `gui_main.d`'s
`writeCodeFile()`/`writeStringsFile()`, matching FLTK's own
`completion_button->value()` check in `Fluid.write_code_files()`/
`Project::write_strings()` -- failure alerts stay unconditional either
way, matching FLTK), "Show Ghosted Group Outlines" (`gui_main.
showGhostedOutline()`, drives `fl.draw.ghostFlatBox` plus a
no-box-group tree-walk -- see `fluid.canvas.ProjectCanvas.draw()`'s
own doc comment for the full mechanism), and "Show Restricted Areas"
(`gui_main.showRestricted()`, drives out-of-bounds/overlap
hatching from `ProjectCanvas.drawOverlay()` -- see that function's own
doc comment). Locale is fully wired to
`fluid.i18n.I18nSettings` (`gui_main.projectI18n()`), a real subsystem
that predates this pass. Shell keeps its pre-existing real wiring
(`fluid/panels/shell_settings.d`), just repositioned to fit the new
narrower single-column dialog width -- every widget it names is
unchanged, only `xywh` moved.

Tab icons (`../icons/*_64.png` in FLTK) are real, copied into
`fluid/panels/pixmaps/` and referenced the same way this project's own
`about_panel.fl`/`fluid_icon.fl` already reference their own bundled
pixmaps (relative to this very directory, not FLTK's sibling
`icons/`, since this port's icons live under `panels/pixmaps/`
alongside everything else `code_writer.d`'s `writeOneImage()` embeds).
Not ported: FLTK's own custom Fluid-app `@fd_beaker`/`@fd_user`/
`@fd_project`/`@fd_file` `fl_add_symbol()` glyphs (hand-drawn C++
callback functions registered under those symbol names, `fluid/app/
Snap_Action.cxx`) -- the Layout tab's storage-location menu items keep
their FLTK text minus that leading symbol. `@fd_zoom` (`fluid/rsrcs
/pixmaps.cxx`) is a real, ported `fl.symbols` glyph
(`fluid.pixmaps`'s own `fdZoom()`) -- the Shell tab's
"open the big code editor" button uses FLTK's real `@+1fd_zoom`
label, which fits
the button's real 22x22 size, unlike a plain `"Zoom..."` text label. A separate, simpler
asset, not an `fl_add_symbol()` glyph at all: the Shell tab's own
per-row list icons (`fd_user.png`/`fd_project.png`, plain bitmaps
copied in alongside the tab icons above, held by the hidden
`shellFdUserBox`/`shellFdProjectBox`) are wired to `fl.browser.
Browser`'s real per-row `icon()`
(`shell_settings.d`'s `shellRefreshList()`).
}
  {
    in_source
    in_header
  }
decl {import fluid;}
  {
    private
    local
  }
decl {import shell_run_window : showShellRunWindow;}
  {
    private
    local
